  "prefLabel": "Ins 901.03 Restriction on Use of Terms “Actuary” or “Actuarial”",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 901.03 Restriction on Use of Terms “Actuary” or “Actuarial”.\n\n(a) No person shall represent themselves as an actuary to the insurance department unless such person is a qualified actuary.\n\n(b) No person shall make any representation to the insurance department in which the term \"actuary\" or \"actuarial\" is used to indicate a degree of professional competence unless such representation was prepared or approved by a qualified actuary.\n\n(c) No person who is a qualified actuary shall make any representations using the terms “actuary” or “actuarial” to the insurance department unless they are qualified to give the actuarial advice therein contained.\n\nSource. #1900, eff 1-1-82; ss by #4287, eff 7-1-87; ss by #5649, eff 7-1-93; ss by #7028, INTERIM, eff 7-1-99, EXPIRES: 10-29-99; ss by #7123, eff 10-29-99; ss by #8965, eff 9-1-07; ss by #10919, eff 9-1-15; ss by #14511, eff 2-7-26, EXPIRES: 2-7-36",
